From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:06:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScript: history sets the location, BroadcastChannel,
 alpha strings

history.pushState and replaceState with a URL now change the document's
location (resolved against it, same origin only, SecurityError
otherwise), and traversal sets it back; YouTube's router navigated to a
video and the location stayed on the search page.  location.search and
hash have their ? and #.  BroadcastChannel (to the page's other channels
of the same name) for YouTube's player.  Computed colours write their
alpha as browsers do (0.05, not 0.0470588).
---
 .../handlers/javascript/duktape/Location.bnd  | 28 +++++++---
 .../handlers/javascript/duktape/Window.bnd    | 45 +++++++++++++++-
 .../handlers/javascript/duktape/webapi.js     | 54 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/netsurf/content/handlers/javascript/duktape/Location.bnd b/netsurf/content/handlers/javascript/duktape/Location.bnd
index a731730..328d0aa 100644
--- a/netsurf/content/handlers/javascript/duktape/Location.bnd
+++ b/netsurf/content/handlers/javascript/duktape/Location.bnd
@@ -318,10 +318,16 @@ getter Location::search()
 
 	nsurl_get(priv->url, NSURL_QUERY, &url_s, &url_l);
 
-	/* if url_s is NULL duk_push_lstring pushes an empty string
-	 * which is correct for this API
-	 */
-	duk_push_lstring(ctx, url_s, url_l);
+	/* "" without one, else with its "?" (nsurl may give it without) */
